WEBVTT

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.980
Taeguk refers to the source of everything in the universe

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.460
and the universal law in which everything continuously goes through cycles

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.700
of creation and destruction.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.820
Pumse Taeguk symbolizes the root principle of universal philosophy

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:47.180
and is constructed by applying the truth inherent in Taeguk's yin and yang principles.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.060
Taeguk Ija stands for Tae of the eight trigrams

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.820
and symbolizes the pond which looks soft on the outside

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.420
but is strong on the inside.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:02.540
Taeguk Ija was designed for the student to train moves in succession

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:06.140
based on advancing the basic moves learned in Taeguk Ija.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.700
We will now take a look at the Pumse of Taeguk Ija.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:01.380
Taeguk Ija consists of one key move, Olgul Jirugi.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:10.480
We will now take a closer look at the key move of Taeguk Ija, Olgul Jirugi.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:17.040
Olgul Jirugi is a move where you thrust your fist in a straight line toward the opponent's philtrum.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.720
Be careful not to let the elbow of your thrusting arm move outward.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.380
That was the key move of Taeguk Ija.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:34.610
We will now connect the moves in succession and take a closer look at each one.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:39.410
The key moves of Taeguk Ija first part consist of

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:43.730
Wen Are Makki, Orun Jirugi, Orun Are Makki,

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:51.330
Orun Are Makki, Wen Jirugi, Orun An Makki, and Wen An Makki.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:57.650
When moving the center of your body forward during Apsogi Are Makki,

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:02.050
control your breath, lower your body and set forward.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:04.290
Then thrust your body with Apgubi.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.250
The moment the foot setting forward touches the ground,

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:12.930
complete the Jirugi simultaneously with the move and breath.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:17.410
When setting your right foot forward during Orun An Makki,

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:21.410
breathe in while moving the center of your body to your left foot.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:24.770
Remove any unnecessary force from both feet

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:31.090
and seek the body's optimal condition to perform the Orun Apsogi and Wen An Makki afterwards.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.690
Cautions for Taeguk Ija.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.930
First part, taking a closer look.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.850
Your torso and arms must spin simultaneously.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:46.130
Move the center of your body and breathe in once the move is complete

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.090
and remove any unnecessary force from your muscles.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:55.220
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Ija first part

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.020
in succession slowly while watching the video.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:13.760
The key moves of Taeguk Ija second part consist of

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.920
Wen Are Makki, Orun Apsogi, and Orun Jirugi.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:23.840
The connection of Apsogi and Jirugi should be made so the momentum gained

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:29.840
after the Apsogi folds the kicking leg, resulting in a natural connection with Jirugi.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.840
When connecting Orgul Makki and the next Orgul Makki,

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.840
the elbow of the arm that protected the face should come out.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:43.540
When connecting Orgul Makki and the next Orgul Makki,

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:47.540
the elbow of the arm that protected the face should come out.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.260
The arm that protected the face should come down first,

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.700
and the first placed on the waist should be raised

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:58.420
so your arms will be crossed at the chest and ready to perform the Orgul Makki.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:02.420
Cautions for Taeguk Ija.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.660
Second part, taking a closer look.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:10.100
Be careful not to let your leg rise above your head when performing Apsogi.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:14.740
It is important that the move connects naturally to Jirugi.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.660
Be careful not to let the natural flow be broken.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.290
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Ija,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.730
second part in succession slowly while watching the video.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:49.940
The key moves of Taeguk Ija, third part, consist of Orun Anmakki and Wen Anmakki.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:54.740
From the Orgul Makki, shift your weight on your right foot,

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:59.620
spin 270 degrees, and perform Doradiki.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.420
When connecting Anmakki, Anmakki, and Doradiki,

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.460
shift your weight on your left foot and spin.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:11.460
Your right arm should face the direction of progress.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:17.380
Spin the pelvis, which is the center axis, then perform Anmakki with the left arm.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.900
Cautions for Taeguk Ija, third part, taking a closer look.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:28.500
Be careful not to raise your right leg too much when performing Doradiki.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:34.880
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Ija,

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.160
third part in succession slowly while watching the video.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:50.000
The key moves of Taeguk Ija, fourth part, consist of Wen Aremakki,

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.960
Orun Aptagi, and Orun Jirugi.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:07:04.690
The three Aptagi and Jirugi moves must all be performed in succession.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:09.460
Pay close attention to the connection of each move.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:17.580
Cautions for Taeguk Ija, fourth part, taking a closer look.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:23.980
The target for Aptagi is in the front, and be careful not to kick above your head.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.910
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Ija,

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:34.190
fourth part in succession slowly while watching the video.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:50.020
This concludes training for Taeguk Ija.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:54.900
We will take another look at the moves and master Pumse.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:44.450
We have looked at the key moves of Taeguk Ija,

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:48.850
and provided thorough explanations for each move and things to watch out for.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:54.900
You will be able to master the correct and delicate details of the moves

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:58.500
if you train with the meaning of Taeguk Ija in mind,

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.140
and focus on strengthening its inner contents.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.100
We will see you again in the Taeguk Samjang video.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:07.940
Thanks for watching.

